[[file:Attribute range icon.png|50px]]
'''Range''' determines how long tears will travel before landing and is represented by a bow and arrow.

{{dlc|nr}} This attribute's name is misleading because Range determines the ''time'' that a shot stays in the air rather than the ''"distance"'' that it travels. The effective Range is calculated based on said travel time, [[Shot Speed]], and [[Tear Falling Speed]]. Range cannot be lowered below 5.0 but has no upper limit. Internally, this attribute is called Tear Height, and also affects the starting height that tears spawn at.
* {{dlc|r}} Range now represents how many tiles a tear will travel. Range cannot be lowered below 1.0, but has no upper limit. Tear Height no longer represents this attribute and no longer affects effective range.

Extremely high Tear Height makes Isaac's tears start so high in the air they can cross over [[obstacles]] as if they were [[spectral tears|spectral]], but they won't go through room walls. Once the tears fall down, they will start hitting obstacles again. This compounds with [[Tear Falling Speed]].

