* {{c|Azazel}}: The mini-Brimstone beam doesn't calculate its Range the same way as normal tear attacks, so his Range stat is misleading. His attack has a much shorter Range than other characters with the same value.
* {{c|Eden}} and {{c|Tainted Eden}}: Range is a random value between 5.0 and 8.0, inclusive.
* {{c|The Forgotten}} and {{c|Tainted Forgotten}}: Their melee attacks don't calculate their Range the same way as normal tear attacks, and their actual attack Range is far less than other characters with the same value.
** {{c|The Soul}}: Tear attack range works normally.
** {{c|Tainted Soul}}: Incapable of firing tears. The range of the thrown Forgotten body is unaffected by Range.
* {{c|Tainted Magdalene}}: The lethal hug is unaffected by Range. Tear attack range works normally.
* {{c|Tainted Samson}}: The melee attack in [[Berserk!|the berserk state]] doesn't calculate its Range in the same way as normal tear attacks, and its actual attack Range is far less than other characters with the same value. Tear attack range for non-berserk state works normally.
* {{c|Tainted Azazel}}: The thin Brimstone beam has unlimited Range, while {{I|Hemoptysis|n}} is not affected by Range, so his Range stat isn't commonly relevant.
